pubDate: 2026-11-22
---

I used to write notes, scripts, life highlights inside a notebook [this one specifically](https://amzn.eu/d/02SpFeKn). It's the best time to embarrass myself on the internet, because why not?

It's not about writing things for people to read (at the end of the day it's going to be read by web scrapers duh) it's mostly about writing things that matter to the world. At least I hope. I hope this gives you a sense of life, reading something a human wrote for fun. 

## What I do 
This is probably where it's more difficult to get into, because it's so complex that I don't even know what I do. Generally I'm a software engineer, full stack dev, IT whatever you want to call me with intent in focusing on.. everything. I can't remember that last time where I was doing nothing, that just puts me in a bad icky mood. I really like solving problems, but I also really really like telling people what to do and how to do it in the most efficient way possible. I like solving problems, and my moto of this year is:
import { defineCollection } from "astro:content";
import { glob } from "astro/loaders";
import { z } from "astro/zod";

export const collections = {
  articles: defineCollection({
    loader: glob({ pattern: "*.md", base: "./src/content/articles" }),
    schema: z.object({
      title: z.string(),
      description: z.string(),
      pubDate: z.coerce.date(),
      // set when an article is meaningfully revised; shown to search engines as dateModified
      updatedDate: z.coerce.date().optional(),
      // topics, used as article:tag and schema.org keywords
      tags: z.array(z.string()).default([]),
      // shows the audio player; needs the mp3 (public/audio/ in dev, R2 in production)
      // and public/narration/<slug>.vtt, recorded with the dev-only "Record timings" button
      narrated: z.boolean().default(false),
      // also serve public/audio/<slug>.original.mp3 (the unprocessed recording) behind a
      // Krisp / Original switch; both files must share the same timings
      originalAudio: z.boolean().default(false),
      // where the article was posted, shown as logos next to the date
      shared: z.array(z.object({ platform: z.enum(["linkedin", "x"]), url: z.url() })).default([]),
      // drafts show in `astro dev` only
      draft: z.boolean().default(false),
    }),
  }),
};

